<div class="p">
  <div>
    <p>
      The Living Set was conceived around the idea that a table is never static: it is living. Alive through movement,
      interaction, atmosphere, and ritual.
      <br>
      <br>

      The name speaks to this constant sense of motion: the passing of objects, the choreography of gathering, the
      shifting glow of candlelight, the quiet theatre that unfolds around a shared table. Each piece is created as an
      object with presence - sculptural forms designed to bring rhythm, tension, and fluidity into a setting.
      <br>
      <br>

      Rooted in a distinctly theatrical sensibility, The Living Set approaches the table as a stage. Silver-plated
      serving pieces, candle holders, and decorative objects become characters within a composition, interacting through
      form, proportion, reflection, and movement. Function exists alongside drama; utility alongside ornament.

      <br>
      <br>
      Balancing sculptural restraint with expressive detail, the brand creates collectible objects intended to elevate
      the rituals of hosting and transform the everyday into something cinematic, intimate, and deeply considered.

      <br>
      <br>
      The Living Set is an exploration of atmosphere through object - where design gives life to the table.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

